<section>
<title>Detailed Description</title>

<para>C-API: File callbacks. </para>



<para>Actually, it&apos;s a data structure to wrap a set of fXXXX (e.g fopen) replacement functions.</para>

<para>The default implementation of the functions utilizes the fXXX functions from the CRT. However, you can supply a custom implementation to <link linkend="_namespace_assimp">Assimp</link> by delivering a custom <link linkend="_structai_file_i_o">aiFileIO</link>. Use this to enable reading from other sources, such as ZIP archives or memory locations. </para>
</section>
